{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the bounded-JSONata subset security fix for #761, reviewed independently at exact head 014296c5035768d57bcac47faa1cf4a72f29735d in a clean detached worktree. The fix is the durable AST-based one I recommended: after jsonata.Compile, validateJSONataAST walks the compiled AST (Expression.AST()) and rejects lambda nodes and any function/partial/apply whose callable is not an allowlisted $variable, via validateJSONataCallable; the old source-text jsonataCallRE/jsonataLambdaRE regexes are removed, and validateJSONataLexicalSource keeps only the asterisk/range lexical checks as defense-in-depth. RuntimeID bumped 4 to 5. VERIFIED both holes are closed at this head:\n- Walker completeness: I dumped v206 parser.go ASTNode and checked every child-bearing field is visited (LHS, RHS, Expression, Procedure, Pattern, Update, Delete, Condition, Then, Else, Body, Expressions, Arguments, Steps, RHSPairs, LHSPairs, RHSTerms/Terms via .Expression, Predicate/Stages via .Expr, Group.LHS pairs); the aux structs Group (only LHS pairs), SortTerm (only Expression), Stage (only Expr) carry no unwalked expression fields. Fail-closed if AST() is not a *ASTNode.\n- Independent reproduction: my original H-NEW-1/H-NEW-2 exploit set (event ~\u003e $keys / $spread / $reverse / $sort / $base64encode, the lambda-synonym doubling program, and a dynamic data-driven callable event ~\u003e event.callable) is now REFUSED by the gate at this head, while the pinned evaluator still parses the syntax — proving the gate rejects, not a parse failure. Allowlisted apply and normal calls still pass (event.session_id ~\u003e $string, $lookup(...), $substring($string(...),0,4)).\n- Builder tests: TestJSONataSubsetRejectsUnboundedExtensionPoints now includes unicode lambda, apply keys/spread/sort/base64encode, and apply of a dynamic callable; TestJSONataSubsetAllowsApplyOperatorForAllowlistedFunction asserts $string via apply remains admitted.\nBattery re-run in the clean worktree: go test ./... 13 packages ok, go test -race ./... zero failures, go vet clean, scripts/demo.sh passes; working tree clean afterwards. All three builder-signed artifacts at 014296c5 cited, internal/profile/compiler.go primary. No required changes. Two non-blocking advisories: (1) the object-wildcard/multiplication exclusion is still lexical (hasUnquotedAsterisk) rather than AST-based — consistent but a future candidate to move onto the same AST walk for uniformity; (2) fold-time evaluation still has no deterministic step/allocation budget (only SetMaxDepth/SetMaxRange/SetMaxTime), so the \u0026-concatenation and :=-binding geometric-growth class from my earlier finding remains reachable within the now-narrower admitted language — the AST gate does not by itself close that, and a step/allocation budget (the long-standing milestone-A B2 item) is still the real fix; worth a tracking note but out of scope for this security request.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:49ebfd2d9e17c5f102f16ae0de3e6bc461f253f9","head":"014296c5035768d57bcac47faa1cf4a72f29735d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:6533a0186bd1f546f4e43a811451a77ba9274cb4\",\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:d0fdb8acfe4e3d0eeca75b57a3803c6e049d4576\",\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:f00b7d79e5c23f275103733720d61fc5d2f3fc99\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:f00b7d79e5c23f275103733720d61fc5d2f3fc99","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}